System Request:	HouseBroker: House Price Recommendation System 
Project Sponsor:	Krishna Vamsi Mada
Business Need:	People who plan to buy or rent a house often struggle to determine whether a listed property price is reasonable. Many rely on guesswork, listing comparisons, or informal opinions, which may not reflect actual market value. As a result, buyers and renters may overpay or miss fair deals.
The title of this project is HouseBroker. It uses price prediction and recommends a price range for people who want to purchase or rent a house. Price prediction is based on attributes such as location, number of rooms, proximity to amenities, accessibility, and similar housing characteristics.
There are already platforms such as Airbnb, NoBroker, and other real estate applications that provide price-related insights. The idea of estimating property value is therefore not new or cutting-edge. The purpose of this project is different. The core objective is to put theory into practice for a realistic demonstration of concepts learned in coursework. Instead of proposing a novel market product, this project demonstrates a real implementation of predictive analytics concepts within a functional system.
Real datasets such as the Boston housing dataset and other publicly available housing datasets will be used to simulate real-world conditions. Using multiple datasets helps represent variation across housing markets and supports realistic system behavior during demonstration.
