•	Display feature influence
•	Upload datasets
•	Train regression models
•	Evaluate model performance
•	Activate selected model
The following sections list the functional and non-functional requirements.

Requirements Definition 
Functional Requirements
1.	An End User inputs location-related variables into the system.
2.	An End User inputs number of rooms.
3.	An End User inputs accessibility-related variables.
4.	An End User inputs proximity indicators to amenities.
5.	An End User inputs additional numeric housing features required by the model.
6.	An End User provides an optional listing price.
7.	An End User submits the complete property profile for analysis.
8.	The system verifies completeness of required housing attributes.
9.	The system validates numeric range of submitted features.
10.	The system converts categorical inputs into numerical representations when necessary.
11.	The system aligns user input with the trained model’s feature structure.
12.	The system standardizes or scales feature values consistent with training configuration.
13.	The system logs input validation results.
14.	The system executes the active regression model using processed input features.
15.	The system computes an estimated property price.
16.	The system calculates an expected price interval based on model residual distribution.
17.	The system compares predicted value with listing price when provided.
18.	The system calculates percentage deviation between predicted price and listing price.
19.	The system assigns pricing status as underpriced, fairly priced, or overpriced.
20.	The system extracts regression coefficients or feature contribution metrics.
21.	The system ranks input features based on contribution magnitude.
22.	The system displays estimated property price.
23.	The system displays calculated price interval.
24.	The system displays pricing status classification.
25.	The system displays influential variables affecting prediction.
26.	A Model Administrator imports housing datasets into the system.
27.	The system performs dataset cleaning by handling missing or inconsistent values.
28.	The system performs feature selection based on statistical relevance.
29.	The system trains regression-based models using prepared datasets.
30.	The system computes evaluation metrics including RMSE and R².
31.	A Model Administrator reviews model evaluation metrics.
32.	A Model Administrator selects and activates a trained model for prediction tasks.
33.	A Model Administrator updates dataset records.
34.	A Model Administrator removes obsolete datasets.
 
Non-Functional Requirements
1.	The system will return price estimation results within a reasonable analytical runtime suitable for interactive evaluation.
2.	The system will complete model training within a demonstrable time window appropriate for regression computation on moderate datasets.
3.	The system will restrict dataset import and model activation functions to Model Administrator accounts.
4.	The system will require authentication before allowing administrative operations.
5.	The system will implement interpretable regression-based prediction techniques.
6.	The system will document model assumptions used in prediction.
7.	The system will present output as estimation guidance rather than financial or legal advice.
8.	The system will acknowledge that prediction reliability depends on dataset representativeness and market stability.
